A||N||5||Iron Duke Wellingsley||ECM bad?  Lousy idle in gear (84 2M4 Automatic)||||1||
Z||000000||Iron Duke Wellingsley||06-11-2001||07:28 PM||||Hi,<P>I have rebuilt my 2.5L engine.  It's stock except for the Compu Cams camshaft:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.racesearch.com/CGI/racesearch_ec.cgi?race_product_id=47373;description_id=1542" TARGET=_blank>http://www.racesearch.com/CGI/racesearch_ec.cgi?race_product_id=47373;description_id=1542</A> <P>When it idles in drive, the vacuum is really low and it flutters.  It sounds like a dragster going "bllllummmppp, bllllummmppp, bllllummmpp, . . ."  It uses tons of gas when it's idling.  You can see the spray and a layer of fuel all over the TBI butterfly and "bowl."  There's a nasty flat spot at 2500 rpm, and at 3000 rpm on the freeway the car surges noticeably.  After this, when you pull off the road it will stall.  <P>The TCC is working: passed brake test at 45mph.  New TPS, Coolant Temp sensor, ignition control module, wires, cap, plugs, rotor, park nuetral switch, battery, alternator, coil, etc.  <P>The ECM is original.  I have been having the idle problem for a while.  All of the replacements including the engine rebuild were made to fix it.<P>But now, I am worried that this camshaft is a bad match for my automatic.  The URL above says it's operating range is 1200 to 5000 rpm.  Idle in drive is 750 rpm.  Is that too low for this camshaft?  <P>On the other hand, this problem has been around longer than the engine, I can't help but wonder if the ECM is to blame.  <P>I've been using the Factory service manuals diagnostic charts, and in several cases it recommends ECM replacement if all else fails.<P>It seems like there are only two ways left to go, put a factory cam back in and/or replace the ECM.<P>I have another spare original ECM for an 1984 automatic.  I will swap it in and then post again.  <P>But, where would you bet the problem is?  ECM or camshaft?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Iron Duke Wellingsley||06-11-2001||09:34 PM||||I put the other original ECM in the car and there is a slight but noticeable improvement.  At 1000 rpms the idle is almost smooth with an occasional burble.  In drive at 750 rpms, the idle is improved, but still rough.<P>I guess the next step is to put miles on the car and see what the ECM can learn.  Somehow, I suspect that the camshaft is too radical . . .<P>Has anyone tried the cam listed at the start of this thread?<P>Is it okay to have a bit lumpy idle when in drive?  It seems like with the low vacuum the car is running rich.  Can it learn to run leaner when idling in gear?<P>Or, did I just put a less bad ECM in the car?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brucepts||06-11-2001||10:38 PM||||Did you do any work to the head and valves or just put a cam in? <P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||06-11-2001||10:58 PM||||I dunno about cams in the computerized cars, but when I was working on my Z28 back in the day and put a new cam in it, that's what it did.. Low idle made it run rough, almost seemed like it was going to stall out. We had to advance the timing slightly. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Iron Duke Wellingsley||06-11-2001||11:19 PM||||The head is stock, but with a professional valve job (added stainless guides on exhaust valves) and new springs (sealed power) and rockers (sealed power).  Everything passed the magnaflux test. The engine runs very smooth above 1000 rpm with no load.  <P>Here's the cam specs<P>operating rpm range : 1200-5200<BR>duration in degrees : advertised in.:260 advertised ex.:260 @.050" in.:212 @.050" ex.:212<BR>lift w/ rocker arms :1.75 rocker arms in:.489", ex:.489"<BR>  <BR>I used the lifters Compu Cams recommended for this cam.  <P>I am going to try advancing the timing a few degrees, probably set for 12 rather than 8.  I'll post again after I try it out.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Brucepts||06-11-2001||11:52 PM||||Did you degree the cam in when u installed it? Might be off there giving you problems. My 2.5 idles like this without a cam in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
